== Overview

Samples:

- Longitudinal mTBI: Had mTBI between T0 and T2 (N = ~200)
    - The group is further divided into label propagated clusters based on how similar their pre-injury, baseline data was to the post-mTBI clustering done in the baseline sample.
- Longitudinal uninjured: Never had mTBI as of T2 (N = ~10k)

Figures:


- #text(fill: purple, [long.png: Side-by-side comparisons between T0 to T2 for CBCL and SDS])
- #text(fill: purple, [long_diff.png: Like long.png, but plotting T2 minus T0 values])
- #text(fill: blue, [preinj_v_change.png: Jitter plots with T0 on x-axis and T2 minus T0 on y-axis])

Comments below are colour-coded based on which plots they are based on.
Outcomes where label propagated cluster associated with longitudinal change in some way are _CAPITALIZED AND ITALICIZED_.

== Internalizing problems

===  Anxious-Depressed

#set text(fill: purple)

The effect of time/injury seems consistent for the mTBI sample.
Predicted cluster did not make much of a difference.
mTBI kids generally worsened at T2, while uninjured kids generally improved.
Restricting the uninjured kids to matched controls will reveal if the difference is due to the injury or pre-injury characteristics.

#set text(fill: blue)

Correlations between pre-injury scores and pre-to-post changes were the same for all groups.
The trend generally shows that higher pre-injury scores are associated with better improvements.

#set text(fill: black)

=== _WITHDRAWN-DEPRESSED_

#set text(fill: purple)

Kids predicted cluster 1 seem to experiencing a more substantial worsening from T0 to T2 than all the other groups.
Predicted cluster 2 had a slight worsening from T0 to T2, and predicted cluster 3 showed no overall change from T0 to T2.
The uninjured kids showed no overall change from T0 to T2.

#set text(fill: blue)

Predicted cluster 1 had a much stronger negative association between preinjury values and T0 to T2 change.
Predicted cluster 1 children with low pre-injury scores generally worsened more from T0 to T2 than the average uninjured child, while predicted cluster 1 children with high pre-injury scores generally recovered much more than the average uninjured child.

#set text(fill: black)

=== _SOMATIC COMPLAINTS_

#set text(fill: purple)

T0 to T2 overall led to no change in predicted cluster 1, while predicted cluster 2 and the uninjured children generally recovered slightly.
Predicted cluster 3 appeared to slightly worsen, but again this was a much smaller sample size than the other groups.

#set text(fill: blue)

Correlation between pre-injury score and T0 to T2 change appear to generally be the same for all groups.

#set text(fill: black)

== Externalizing problems

=== Rule-breaking

#set text(fill: purple)
All groups appeared to generally get better from T0 to T2.
Uninjured children showed the greatest improvement from T0 to T2, but the difference in improvements across all groups was similar.

#set text(fill: blue)

Correlation between pre-injury score and T0 to T2 change appear to generally be the same for all groups.
#set text(fill: black)

=== Aggressive

#set text(fill: purple)

Children in predicted cluster 1 worsened from T0 to T2 noticeably, while all other groups generally improved from the T0 to T2 timepoint.

#set text(fill: blue)

However, correlation between pre-injury score and T0 to T2 change appear to generally be the same for all groups.
The previously described difference between predicted cluster 1 and the other groups may just be a result of the 

Group 1 had the biggest increase
Group 1 had the biggest baseline
Higher baselines lead to bigger decreases



#set text(fill: black)

